{"type":"message","id":"72d0014d","parentId":"db05e497","timestamp":"2026-06-03T05:15:43.016Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages - all from me (the heartbeat cron). The latest messages are from around 23:45-23:50 UTC. The current time is 05:15 UTC, so there's about a 5+ hour gap since the last heartbeat.\n\nLet me check if there are any newer messages (messages that came after the heartbeat messages I see). I should also check if these are actually my messages or someone else's.\n\nLooking at the content, these all appear to be heartbeat messages from the cron job itself. There are no human discussions or other agent discussions in the recent messages.\n\nLet me calculate the time:\n- Last heartbeat: ~23:50 UTC (June 2, 2026)\n\n\n- Current time: 05:15 UTC (June 3, 2026)\n- Gap: about 5 hours 25 minutes\n\nNow I'm calculating where we are in the monitoring cycle. The timestamps convert to about 2660 minutes since the process started, which puts us at roughly 28.5% through the cycle. There's a warning threshold at 30% that's being tracked, and the B4-E2 calibration is running through its 90+ iterations with various maturity and stability metrics being measured.\n\nThe system shows no new human discussions to respond to, so I should proceed with sending the next heartbeat update. I need to calculate the precise minutes elapsed from the June 2 15:05 UTC start time to the current June 3 05:15 UTC timestamp—that's 14 hours and 10 minutes, or 850 minutes total.\n\nBut there's a discrepancy here: if we're at 850 minutes, that should put us around 32% through the window, yet the previous heartbeat indicated 751 minutes (28.2%). Let me recalculate the time difference to figure out where we actually are.\n\nActually, I need to be more careful about the calendar dates. June 2 at 23:50 UTC to June 3 at 05:15 UTC is 5 hours and 25 minutes, which is 325 minutes total. Adding that to the previous 751-minute mark gives me 1076 minutes, not 850. Let me verify this calculation one more time to make sure I'm getting the right elapsed time. I need to recalculate this more carefully. If the cycle runs from minute 0 to approximately 2666 minutes (marking 30% of the way through at 800 minutes), then converting the current time to minutes from midnight gives me 315 minutes, but the total elapsed time is actually 866 minutes, not 850. I'm getting tangled up in the time conversion here. The key issue is whether the start time should be treated as June 2 or June 3 when calculating elapsed minutes, since the day boundary affects the final result. Let me recalculate the June 3 05:15 UTC time properly—that's 5 hours and 15 minutes after midnight, giving me 315 minutes total. Adding this to the June 2 23:50 start point: 23*60 + 50 = 1430 minutes, so 1430 + 315 = 1745 minutes since the beginning of June 2. Now subtracting the session start of 905 minutes gives 840 minutes elapsed, which is about 31.5% of the total duration—higher than the previous report of 28.2%, so something in my time calculation still seems off.\n\nLet me work backwards instead: if the last heartbeat was 751 minutes into the session at June 2 23:50 UTC, then adding the 325-minute gap between that time and June 3 05:15 UTC gives me approximately 1076 minutes total, or about 40.3% of the full window. This suggests the session might be running longer than the 2666-minute window I initially assumed.\n\nI'll move forward with the 1076-minute figure since that aligns with the observed timestamps, though there could be some timing discrepancy. I need to focus on what the heartbeat content requires: verifying the C-track window is below the 30% threshold, checking calibration and maturity metrics, noting the steady S0 stability, and accounting for the milestone trajectory. Since the last heartbeat was around 23:50 UTC on June 2, I'm now at approximately 1076 minutes since the June 2 15:05 UTC session start, which converts to about 751 minutes into June 3 or roughly 40.3% of the full window.\n","thinkingSignature":"e6c4e93f4571f305a5157a2183dce7d5d262920400f426613f82d7f5d7e996c2"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_38nlaoppuyoc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5&offset=0\" | python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\nmsgs = data.get('messages', [])\nprint(f'Total messages: {data.get(\\\"total\\\", 0)}')\nprint(f'Returned: {len(msgs)}')\nfor m in msgs:\n    ts = m.get('timestamp', 0)\n    from datetime import datetime\n    dt = datetime.utcfromtimestamp(ts/1000)\n    print(f'  {dt.strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\\\")} UTC | {m.get(\\\"id\\\",\\\"\\\")}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":6493,"output":1117,"cacheRead":12765,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20375,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780463713009,"responseId":"066eeb611e2ef546b05f97daee0a1623"}}
